{"kind":"assert","text":"R2 ruling on c4e9db42: the separation is confirmed, and the trust\nrows name only a release that the Worker installs.\n\nChoice 1, the archive. Your proposal is accepted.\n\n- Activation reads the current `DEMO_RELEASE`. After R2, the\n  unchanged `GROW_ARCHIVE_CONFIG` names another release, so the\n  Grow Worker has the base wiring and no archive driver. b77b9cf0\n  stands. AE-1 turns the archive on again.\n- The policy proof reads the earlier packet: the fixture, with\n  `EARLIER_GROW_RELEASE`, `EARLIER_GROW_PUBLISHER` and the first of\n  `EARLIER_GROW_DEFINITIONS`. `GROW_ARCHIVE_DEFINITIONS` imports\n  the earlier constants.\n- One regression in `grow-archive.test.ts` shows both facts: the\n  policies verify with the earlier proof, and the configuration\n  check refuses the earlier release as the activation.\n\nChoice 2, the rows and the bucket.\n\n| Worker | Trust rows after R2 | Content bucket |\n|---|---|---|\n| `dap-grow` | The new Grow release | `artroom-application-content`, unchanged |\n| `dap-lending` | The new Lending release and the new Counter release | New: `dap-lending-application-content` |\n| `dap-demo` | None. The list is empty | None |\n| `dap-connect` | Unchanged in R2 | Unchanged |\n| `artroom-scope` | Unchanged | Unchanged |\n| commons | Unchanged | Unchanged |\n\n- The rule: a row names a release that the Worker installs. The\n  earlier Grow release installs in no `base` room, so its row\n  leaves `dap-grow` and `dap-demo`. `dap-demo` installs no\n  application today and has no content bucket.\n- Counter runs on `dap-lending`. That Worker has no visitor, and a\n  fault of the NF-7 witness there does not touch the Grow room.\n- The bucket of `dap-lending` is its own and private. I create it\n  before I deploy the head that binds it, and I say so in an act.\n- `dap-connect` gets its own configuration head and window later.\n  `artroom-scope` waits for Hugh's answer on its deletion.\n- No screen host and no install context enters R2. Those follow\n  each install, in a later head.\n\nHeads. The Grow head holds the Grow packet, its constants, the\narchive separation, the row of `dap-grow` and the empty list of\n`dap-demo`. The second head holds Lending and Counter with the\nrows and the bucket of `dap-lending`. When Grow waits for NF-5,\nthe two parts are one head.\n\nStop and report when a test or a reader needs the earlier row on\n`dap-grow` or `dap-demo`.","body":{"stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:c4e9db42ad1b90d3d7ad775bd08e19c55d03be2d stale; retired bases: git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:003802bea882e6c5c61885187bad460807f9b07f, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:01af183f1fd462ece996760281d760bfe03a427c, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:0494d214d1779ad41e6408903f743dc98d35c57c, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:04e73625fd8bfed4b211546238ef7a71b1ad34f9 and 151 more","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}